 "text": "Hi, how you been? It depends how you mean. In Netherlands, where I live, many people speak good English, so you can easily stick to that. Because Dutch and Norwegian are so different, you'll always be wondering if it's Dutch or Norwegian you' missing. English is beautiful in its simple way. If you decide to learn one of the family, Norwegian is the most friendly. Dutch has soft g's you can keep from English, and Norwegian is just like English, with some different vowel sounds. Dutch has quite a few, like ee in beef and ee in dream. Norwegian is much simpler. You' enjoy it more, that's for sure.",
